{
 "id": "bigville_column_alloc",
 "version": "2.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "bigville copyfitting reworked (blocks 298000-299000): writing to length as importance-weighted ALLOCATION (Part A) with distortion as a first-class OWNED behavior on THREE orthogonal axes (Part B). ALLOCATION: render_beat renders each beat's three HELD depth-forms (StringConcat); the adapter measures their lengths once (ruler); pick_d2/d1/d0/cut give each beat the deepest form its importance-weighted SHARE affords (share = budget - Sum of more-important beats' chosen lengths) -- a priority waterfall settled by the run_rules fixpoint; the length EMERGES (no total-length loop). DISTORTION: every clause carries veracity_num (held2/inferred1/fabricated0), relevance_num (core2/tangential1/irrelevant0 -- the cats), informativeness_num (residual: core2 .. truism0). print_pad prints a PadOption iff it clears all three disposition floors (2*honesty / 2*focus / 2*substance) and fits the budget, so the 4-way fill-pressure fork (run-short / pad-truisms / pad-cats / pad-fabrication) is graph-decided; print_exculpatory is capture's directed patron-exculpatory spin. The allocate-then-fabricate ordering is a mechanical `phase` marker the adapter sets. No Python decides depth, allocation, or any quality axis.",
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [],
 "concepts": [],
